  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe center of an upper level ridge shifts toward the Four Corners \nregion by midweek, where it shall meander through much of the Long \nTerm period. Each afternoon will feature highs mainly in the upper\n90s, with triple digit heat near/along the river valleys. Meanwhile,\novernight lows shall settle into the mid 60s/70s. Most locations \nlook to remain dry through the period. Models indicate a few \nshortwave impulses may round the eastern edge of the ridge late \nthis week and into the weekend. These could bring isolated showers\nor storms to portions of our region, mainly favoring the higher \nterrain. However, we shall see what becomes of these impulses as \nwe head through the week.",
